cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "diskvert: 1D vertical structure of magnetic accretion disks"
message: |
  If you use this software, please cite it using the
  metadata from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Dominik
    family-names: Gronkiewicz
    email: gronki@camk.edu.pl
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5325-7705'
    affiliation: CAMK PAN
repository-code: 'https://github.com/gronki/diskvert/'
abstract: |
    Code to compute 1D vertical structure of magnetic accretion disks around black holes.
    Solves coupled equations of hydrostatic equilibrium, energy balance, radiative transfer,
    and magnetic flux balance using a relaxation method. Suitable for modeling accretion
    disks in galactic black hole binaries and active galactic nuclei with self-consistent
    warm coronae.
keywords:
  - X-ray
  - Active Galactic Nuclei
  - Astrophysics
  - Soft X-ray Excess
  - Relaxation
  - accretion
  - accretion disks
  - radiative transfer
  - magnetic fields
  - instabilities
